7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]launch_control_alias_history.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/launch_control_alias_history.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-n8[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-n8/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Record the alias resolution trail and its origin at launch[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]provenance[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]provenance: make alias resolution return the ordered trail of alias hops[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]it traversed, give LaunchSelection that trail plus the origin of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]request (directive vs no-directive default vs no alias), and persist [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`model_alias_trail` and `model_alias_origin` into agent_meta.json and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt-step markers at every launch, reconcile, re-exec, and follow-up [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]write site.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core — alias projection, schema 22, and the alias-history[bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]query[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: in the sase-core repo, add the alias trail/origin to AgentMetaWire[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and PromptStepMarkerWire, project each run's trail into a new normalized[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent_artifact_model_aliases table under artifact-index schema 22 with a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record_json re-projection migration that backfills legacy rows, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expose a bounded `query_agent_alias_history` PyO3 binding that returns [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-alias groups with truncation counts and a directive-stripped prompt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snippet.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python wire mirror, facade call, and skew probes[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]wire[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire: mirror the new core contract on the Python side — alias [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trail/origin on the marker wires, a new agent_alias_history_wire module [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with its to_dict/from_dict helpers, a `query_agent_alias_history` facade[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]function under the artifact-index operation lock — and extend the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase_core_rs validator so a stale wheel fails loudly instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]returning empty history.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The per-alias history limit config field[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]config[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]config: add `llm_provider.model_alias_history_limit` (default 10, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]minimum 1) to the JSON schema, the shipped default config commentary, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and a validated accessor, and document it in the configuration and LLM [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]references.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Frontend-neutral alias-history adapter[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]adapter[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wire, config[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adapter: add the presentation-neutral adapter that composes the core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]query with the configured limit, resolves ProjectSpec keys to configured[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project names, classifies each run's provenance into direct / [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]via-another-alias / default / unrecorded, and returns typed view models [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with the group truncation state.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The Launch Control agent-history panel and its `H` keymap[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]panel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adapter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel: add the `H` binding and its context-aware footer entries to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Launch Control, build the pop-up panel (title summary, grouped rows, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]two-line detail strip, footer) on the panel's existing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]worker/navigation/jump machinery, add full-prompt view, copy, load-more,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh, and hidden-toggle actions, style it alongside the other Launch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Control panels, and document it in the ACE reference.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]PNG goldens for the history panel[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]visual[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]visual: add deterministic fixtures and PNG snapshot coverage for the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]history panel's populated, grouped, truncated, legacy-provenance, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]empty states, and confirm no existing Launch Control golden moves.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Raise the sase-core-rs dependency window[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]floor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel, visual[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]floor: after the sase-core release publishes, move both bounds of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core-rs version window in pyproject.toml to the release carrying [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact index schema 22, and confirm the exhaustive gate passes against[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the published wheel.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Acceptance against real agent history[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after provenance, floor[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify: exercise the panel against the real machine-local artifact index[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]— a legacy-only alias, a freshly launched alias, a bucket, a truncated [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]alias, and an alias with no runs — and confirm the migration backfilled [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]without a full rebuild.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-n8","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-n8.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-n8.1"},"source_run_id":"run-f58a1ff1618eace9c1bbaf6c926b51b8","started_at":"2026-08-16T15:41:48.809345+00:00","state":"active"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.6","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.7","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.8","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.9","bbugyi200.athena.sase-n8.land"]}
